			"Message": "style(Output): Strip redundant blank lines and tighten tsconfig exclude\n\nRemove blank lines inserted by the previous blanket-formatting pass — every import group, interface property, object entry, and function body in Source/Apply, Source/ESBuild, Source/Plugin, Source/Polyfill, and Source/Service now omits the vertical whitespace between consecutive sibling statements. The convention shifts to separating logical blocks only (e.g. between import groups vs. between every import).\n\nAdd explicit exclude paths to tsconfig.json for Source/Polyfill/Child/Process, Source/Polyfill/File/Protocol, Source/Polyfill/File/System, Source/Polyfill/IPC/Renderer, Source/Polyfill/Native/Module, Source/Polyfill/Shared/Process, Source/Polyfill/Process, Source/Service/Tauri/Main/Process, and Source/Plugin/Transform/Replace/Product — these directories contain runtime shims or platform-specific services whose ambient types should not participate in the Output package's own TypeScript compilation.\n\nReformat README.md tables with proper GFM alignment rows and reflow DeepDive.md paragraph breaks to match the 100-char line target, keeping documentation in sync with the refined style.\n\nZero semantic changes to runtime behaviour.",
			"SHA": "f75492cb865a156ec8da995dc04866798a0022d2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:11:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				343,
				94
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Apply consistent blank-line formatting across all source files\n\nNormalize whitespace across the entire Output source tree — every file in Source/Apply, Source/ESBuild, Source/Plugin, Source/Polyfill, and Source/Service now follows a uniform blank-line convention. Each import statement, interface property, object literal entry, and function body is separated by a single blank line, and shell case clauses are re-indented with one level per arm.\n\nThis is a formatting-only pass with zero semantic changes: every transform, polyfill, copy plugin, service shim, and pipeline entry behaves identically at runtime. The consistent layout reduces cognitive friction for contributors and ensures the Prettier/ESLint pass does not produce per-file churn going forward.",
			"SHA": "624abb46f475f5b266f2aca5d0ff843e8f8c89ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:06:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				343,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expose BulkEdit service and gate onView on * settlement\n\nExpose `IBulkEditService` as `Services.BulkEdit` in the CEL ExposeAccessor so that Sky's `sky://workspace/applyEdit` bridge can use the workbench's transactional edit applier for combined text edits and file operations within a single undo group, rather than falling back to per-model edits.\n\nRefine the `activateByEvent` monkey-patch for `onView:<viewId>` events to operate in three phases: before the `*` activation pass has started, the original call is forwarded so lazily-activated view extensions still activate; while `*` is in flight, the in-flight promise is returned so the pane waits for the bulk pass instead of issuing its own Cocoon round-trip; after `*` has settled (even on rejection), the call resolves immediately since every contribution matching `onView:X` was already pulled in by the bulk pass. This prevents extension sidebar panes from hanging forever at the bare `pre/index.html` chrome when Cocoon's RequestRoutingHandler does not short-circuit per-view events.\n\nMove the `output` channel out of `FireAndForgetChannels` in the Tauri process service: `output:registerLogger` and `output:createOutputChannel` callers expect a handle or acknowledgment back, and the channel is low-frequency enough to round-trip through Mountain.\n\nThe `*` activation now tracks both the in-flight promise and a settled flag, and an `IBulkEditService` reference is available for workspace edit bridging.",
			"SHA": "9cefbc3b57bc7fd8e148635c0c649a9efc087127"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:36:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				343,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Expand README with Security, License, Changelog sections and fix file paths\n\nAdd three new top-level sections to the Output README: a Security table documenting the four-layer deterministic-build security model (fixed outputs, plugin AST isolation, polyfill boundaries, compiler process separation), a License section asserting the CC0-1.0 public-domain dedication, and a Changelog section linking to the newly introduced CHANGELOG.md.\n\nCorrect the project structure tree and component table to match actual file paths: Copy plugin lives at Source/Plugin/Copy.ts (not a directory), Transform plugin has 30+ sub-modules (not 20+), Child Process, Native Module, and Process polyfills point to their real entry files, Asset/Style/ gains Editor and Terminal GPU layer sub-directories, and CHANGELOG.md is listed in the root tree. Expand the API Reference with six source-file links. Fix the System Architecture heading by removing the stray em-quad entity and update the Mermaid diagram emoji for Sky (🌌 → ☀️) and Wind (🍃 → 🌬️). Add `title=\"Star\"` attribute to the star badge img tag for accessibility.",
			"SHA": "8798b8de4284383a018b0db4c7fbc41921f5fc1f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:19:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				343,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Replace polling loop with event-driven extension activation\n\nRemove the `ScheduleFire` function that used a 50 ms `setTimeout` followed by a 200 ms `setInterval` (up to 24 attempts — ~4.8 s worst-case) to wait for `__CEL_SERVICES__` to be populated before firing `activateByEvent(\"onStartupFinished\")` and `activateByEvent(\"*\")`.\n\nReplace with an event-driven approach:\n- A module-level `Fired` boolean ensures exactly-once semantics regardless of how the immediate check and the `cel:services-ready` listener race.\n- `FireOnce` checks the flag and calls `FireActivationEvents()` a single time.\n- Immediately checks `Land[\"__CEL_SERVICES__\"]` to handle the case where services are already available before this polyfill runs.\n- Listens for the `cel:services-ready` custom event dispatched by `ExposeAccessor` on window, replacing the polling interval. The listener uses `{ once: true }` for automatic cleanup.\n\nThis eliminates unnecessary timer churn, reduces activation latency from up to ~4.8 s to single-event-loop-tick, and simplifies the control flow by relying on the existing event signal rather than polling.",
			"SHA": "151f68c8c5492b46816b41c5dba621c19bdf62b2"
		}
	],
